  "notes": [
    "J1211+1437 is retained as the Galactic-unbound/HVS candidate because its measured Galactic rest-frame velocity exceeds the local escape velocity for the standard Allen & Santillan potential, although the paper also explores an alternative bound population-II interpretation. The designation \"J1211+2423\" appears twice at T:p7-b6 in discussion of the dark-halo analysis; no such target occurs in the supplied tables, and the context concerns J1211+1437, so it is treated as a typographical error rather than a separate star or identifier.",
    "J1211+1437: The RA and Dec are decoded from the SDSS source identifier SDSSJ121150.27+143716.2 because the paper does not provide a separate numeric coordinate table for J1211+1437. No parallax, target galactocentric radius, or bound/unbound probabilities are reported for this star."
